+PHI handling & air-gapped pilot guidance (El Camino Hospital)
+
+Purpose:
+- Ensure PHI is protected during pilots by running workloads in a dedicated VPC/air‑gapped environment and using de‑identified data for any external collaboration.
+
+Controls (must be implemented before pilot)
+1) Dedicated VPC / network isolation
+   - Provision a dedicated VPC (see terraform/vpc_airgap) with no Internet Gateway.
+   - Allow only necessary egress via approved VPC Endpoints (S3, ECR, KMS) or tightly controlled NAT/proxy.
+   - Peering to hospital networks requires documented approvals and flow logs.
+
+2) Data minimization & de-identification
+   - Use the DEID pipeline to remove direct identifiers (name, SSN, MRN), hash or tokenise reversible IDs only if strictly required.
+   - Only de‑identified or synthetic datasets may leave hospital-controlled networks for external pilots.
+   - Keep original PHI in hospital-controlled storage (not in Aegis cloud) unless a BAA and appropriate controls in place.
+
+3) Access & logging
+   - Use hospital SSO/SCIM for access; limit admin roles.
+   - Enable VPC Flow Logs, S3 access logs and Vault audit logging (send to hospital SIEM).
+
+4) Approvals
+   - Data export for external partners requires explicit Data Use Agreement + Legal/Compliance approval and signed BAA.
+
+DEID tool
+- Use scripts/deid/deidentify.py (simple starter) and validate with clinical informatics before use.
+
