+# Runbook: Human-in-the-loop clinical approval (require clinician confirmation)
+
+Purpose:
+- Ensure any high‑impact clinical model action (treatment recommendation, automated alert that triggers invasive action) requires human clinician approval before action is taken.
+
+Flow:
+1. CI publishes model & evidence bundle and marks promotion as "requires_hil".
+2. n8n HIL workflow (n8n/workflows/hil_approval_workflow.json) notifies Clinical Reviewers (SSO-backed).
+3. Reviewer completes checklist and approves via n8n UI or integrated SSO approval button.
+4. n8n calls receipt_signer to sign the approval receipt; signed receipt is pushed to Rekor and attached to model evidence bundle.
+5. CI/Deployment pipeline resumes and deploys model only if signed receipt present and Gatekeeper pre-load checks pass.
+
+Logging & monitoring:
+- Log every approval event to MLflow run metadata and central audit S3. Monitor HIL approval latency and manual override counts.
+- Report: weekly HIL audit showing approvals, approver identities, run IDs and timestamps.
+
+Clinical safety guidance:
+- Models are advisory by default. Any recommendation that could change clinical action MUST present an approval UI to clinician and require explicit confirmation.
+- Keep a record of clinician confirmation in the EHR when model recommendation leads to clinical action.
+
+Emergency bypass:
+- Only available via documented multi-person authorization (two approvers) and must be recorded with rationale. Use n8n run to produce signed receipts for bypass.
+
