+# Runbook: Signing key compromise & immediate revocation (BYOK/HSM)
+
+Immediate actions (first 60 minutes)
+1. Revoke or disable signing key access in Vault (remove policies that grant transit/sign). See scripts/vault/emergency_revoke_signing_key.sh
+2. Create a new transit signing key and start a rotation (scripts/vault/transit_rotate.sh).
+3. Publish notice internally and notify Legal/Compliance/Clinical Ops.
+4. Identify artifacts signed after suspected compromise time window and mark them as untrusted in the registry.
+5. If necessary, publish "superseding" Rekor entries or evidence bundles indicating revocation (coordinate with Legal).
+
+Post-incident actions
+- Rotate keys across other environments, run re-signing plan for critical artifacts, conduct root cause analysis and engage HSM vendor if applicable.
+- Update incident report and notify external auditors if required by regulations.
+
